# The Hearth (prompt 08 §2): arriving, waking, the companions' talks. Conditions read the Hearth's
# variables (magic/hearth.py: fatigue, band, slept, ate, skipped_sleeps, burnout, visits,
# beaten.<guardian>, letters). Edit freely: docs/WRITING.md.

== hearth_arrival ==
[scene hearth]
Grimoire: A fire, a pot, a roof of branches. The Hearth. Nothing here needs a query until you want one.
<<if band == "tired" or band == "exhausted" or band == "spent">>
Grimoire: Your page is shorter tonight. Sleep would give the rows back.
<<endif>>

== hearth_woke ==
[scene hearth]
Grimoire: You fainted on the field. Someone carried you here. The ink stopped swimming.
Marta Quill: You went down like a sack of letters. Sit. Eat. The road will wait for once.

== marta_talk ==
[scene hearth]
<<if burnout>>
Marta Quill: I am fine. I am fine. I just need to sit down for... a minute. Or a night.
Marta Quill: Do not tell the post office. They would send someone faster.
<<elif skipped_sleeps >= 1>>
Marta Quill: We did not sleep last time either. My legs have started writing me complaints.
<<elif fatigue > 0.6>>
Marta Quill: You look like a ledger nobody has read in a year. Sleep. I will watch the pot.
<<elif ate>>
Marta Quill: That was a real dinner. Sitting down. My children would not believe it.
<<else>>
Marta Quill: I carry what fits in the bag. Four letters, never five. Five and one gets wet.
Marta Quill: Your book has the same rule, I think. Four rows. Pick the ones that matter.
<<endif>>

== marta_leave ==
<<if not slept>>
Marta Quill: No sleep? Good. Good! We can make the next village by dawn. Probably.
<<endif>>
